---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { contact } from "../data/site";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Money Door FX Academy collects, uses, stores and deletes your personal information, including your rights under India's DPDP Act 2023."
  lastUpdated="August 4, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how Money Door FX Academy ("we", "us") collects, uses, stores and
    deletes personal information when you visit our website, register with us, or contact us.
  </p>
  <p>
    Because we are based in Chennai, India and most of the people who register with us are in
    India, we handle personal data in line with the
    <strong>Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 ("DPDP Act")</strong>. Under that Act you
    are the <em>Data Principal</em> and we are the <em>Data Fiduciary</em> — the party responsible
    for what happens to your data.
  </p>

  <h2>What We Collect</h2>
  <p>When you register through our Join Now form, we collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Full name</strong> — so we can address you personally.</li>
    <li><strong>Email address</strong> — to send your confirmation and to reply to you.</li>
    <li><strong>Phone number</strong> — to contact you about the program you're interested in, including via WhatsApp.</li>
    <li><strong>Country, state/region and city</strong> — so we can suggest sessions in a workable time zone and know which market rules apply to you.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We also automatically record, when you submit the form:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your <strong>IP address</strong> and <strong>browser user-agent</strong>, kept solely as a security measure to detect and block automated abuse of the form.</li>
    <li>The <strong>date and time</strong> of your submission, which is also our record of your consent.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Separately, we may collect basic aggregated analytics (pages visited, general region, device
    type). This is not linked to your registration record.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do <strong>not</strong> collect financial information, trading account credentials, or
    payment details through this website. We never ask for your broker password or trading account
    login, and you should never send them to us.
  </p>

  <h2>Why We Collect It, and On What Basis</h2>
  <p>
    We process your data on the basis of the <strong>consent</strong> you give by ticking the box
    on the registration form. We use it only to:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Contact you about our trading education programs and help you choose a starting point.</li>
    <li>Send you the confirmation email for your registration.</li>
    <li>Keep a record of who has registered and when they consented.</li>
    <li>Protect the form against spam and automated abuse.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal information, and we do not share it with our
    referral partners. If you choose to click through to a partner from our
    <a class="text-gold-400 underline" href="/partnerships/">Trading Partners</a> page and sign up with
    them, that is a separate relationship between you and that company, governed by their privacy
    policy — we do not pass them your details.
  </p>

  <h2>Who Else Processes It</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Our email provider</strong> — delivers your confirmation email and the internal notification to our team.</li>
    <li><strong>Our hosting provider</strong> — runs the website and its registration endpoint.</li>
    <li><strong>Our spam-protection provider</strong> — verifies that form submissions come from a person rather than a script.</li>
    <li><strong>Our records store</strong> — holds the registration list our team works from.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These providers process only what they need to perform their function and are not permitted to
    use your data for their own purposes. Some of them operate servers outside India.
  </p>

  <h2>How Long We Keep It</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Registration details</strong> — kept while we are in contact with you and for up to <strong>24 months</strong> after our last meaningful contact, then deleted.</li>
    <li><strong>Enrolled students</strong> — kept for the duration of the program and for up to <strong>5 years</strong> afterwards, to support alumni queries and to meet record-keeping obligations.</li>
    <li><strong>IP address and user-agent</strong> — kept for <strong>90 days</strong> for abuse prevention, then discarded.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If you ask us to delete your data sooner, we will — see below.</p>

  <h2>Your Rights Under the DPDP Act</h2>
  <p>You have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Access</strong> — ask what personal data we hold about you and how we've used it.</li>
    <li><strong>Correction</strong> — have inaccurate or incomplete data corrected or completed.</li>
    <li><strong>Erasure</strong> — ask us to delete your data, unless we're legally required to keep it.</li>
    <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> — as easily as you gave it. Withdrawing consent stops future processing; it does not undo processing already carried out lawfully.</li>
    <li><strong>Grievance redressal</strong> — raise a complaint with us and receive a response.</li>
    <li><strong>Nominate</strong> — name someone to exercise these rights on your behalf if you die or become incapacitated.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to Request Deletion or Exercise a Right</h2>
  <p>
    Email
    <a class="text-gold-400 underline" href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>
    with the subject line <strong>"Data Request"</strong>, from the email address you registered
    with, and tell us what you want us to do. You can also simply reply to any email you've had
    from us and ask.
  </p>
  <p>
    We will respond within <strong>30 days</strong>. We may ask you to confirm your identity first,
    so that nobody else can access or delete your data by pretending to be you.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Our programs are intended for adults. We do not knowingly collect personal data from anyone
    under 18. If you believe a child has registered with us, contact us and we will delete the
    record.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    Your data is transmitted over an encrypted connection and access to our registration records is
    restricted to the people who need it. No system is perfectly secure, but if a breach affects
    your personal data we will notify you and the Data Protection Board of India as the DPDP Act
    requires.
  </p>

  <h2>Grievance Officer</h2>
  <p>
    If you are unhappy with how we've handled your data or your request, contact our grievance
    contact at
    <a class="text-gold-400 underline" href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>. If you
    remain dissatisfied, you may escalate the matter to the
    <strong>Data Protection Board of India</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with
    an updated "Last updated" date.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy can be sent to
    <a class="text-gold-400 underline" href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>, or via
    our <a class="text-gold-400 underline" href="/join/">Join Now page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
